  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/sim/src/solid_rest.rs`: store an orientation-free CCW XY angular sector on each boundary `Claim` (keeping `Claim` at 40 bytes). Settle multiple non-coplanar bare-boundary plane groups at one Z level by angular multiplicity: emit 1 crossing when any open angular sector has odd group multiplicity (a manifold meridian seam, cone apex or rim), and 0 when every sector has even multiplicity (a grazing V-root or overhang fold). Keep single coplanar groups at 1 crossing.\n- `crates/sim/src/solid_rest_tests.rs`: move the `solid_rest` unit tests to a sibling file (400-line law) and add parity pins for a revolved meridian seam, cone apex, grazing V-root and `Claim` size.\n- `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/scan_turned.rs` and `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/scan_hidden.rs`: check strict entry into the open recess `(p, roof)` in `TurnedBand::excuses` instead of inflating the recess and band by `+/-reach`. A pass ending at a neck step (`Z20..Z60`) or starting at the neck top (`Z63..Z78`) no longer claims the neck floor; any pass that enters or bridges `(p, roof)` still owns that floor and convicts.\n- `crates/sim/tests/turned_hidden_rest.rs` and `crates/app/tests/turning_hidden_floor.rs`: pin Profile Finish and zero-leave Profile Rough over a cone, a neck (`Z60..Z63`) and M10x1.5 V grooves, plus negative pins that a pass stopping inside the neck still blocks the post.\n- `docs/decisions/2880-profile-finish-neck-thread.md`: record the design decision and rejected alternatives.\n- `crates/motion/tests/finish3d.rs`: correct the convex-cap heavy test. Preserve the gouge and refused-plunge checks. Pin one material interval at four meridians, judged hidden rest within tolerance, and no false envelope warning.\n\n## Cause\n\nTwo separate defects in `camcraft-sim` caused the two false rest readings in #2880:\n\n1. On a 64-segment revolved thread, lattice columns on the 45-degree meridian (`x == y`) lie on the shared edge of two non-coplanar flank facets. `solid_rest::crossings_from_claims` emitted one crossing per non-coplanar boundary group (two crossings per flank), which inverted solid/air parity inside every V-groove and exposed the downward-facing upper flank as a hidden top (`0.7028 mm rest`).\n2. `TurnedBand::excuses` inflated the open recess `[p, roof]` and band by `+/-reach` (`+/-(r + floor)`). A cone pass ending at `Z60` (or a thread pass starting at `Z63`) therefore claimed the `Z60..Z63` neck floor (`0.2435 mm rest`), even though no non-gouging tangent ball centre can sit outside the open recess `(60, 63)`.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n- `solid_rest::tests::revolved_meridian_edge_and_v_root_keep_true_parity`\n- `solid_rest::tests::claim_stays_forty_bytes`\n- `stock_sim::scan_turned::tests::a_pass_stopping_at_a_neck_step_does_not_own_the_neck_recess`\n- `turned_hidden_rest::thread_valleys_and_neck_step_at_window_edge_are_not_false_rest`\n- `turning_hidden_floor::profile_finish_over_cone_neck_and_thread_posts`\n- `finish3d::overhang_entries_are_refused_without_false_hidden_rest`\n- `stock_sim::hidden_rest_surfaces_under_a_ceiling` (true hidden-rest control)\n\nRed before fix:\n- `full_z20_z78`: `finish envelope near move 20: 0.0117 mm gouge, 0.7028 mm rest`\n- `cone_z20_z60`: `finish envelope near move 7: 0.0062 mm gouge, 0.2477 mm rest`\n- `rough0_z20_z78`: `finish envelope near move 19855: 0.0117 mm gouge, 0.7028 mm rest`\n\nMutations on `turned_hidden_rest::thread_valleys_and_neck_step_at_window_edge_are_not_false_rest`:\n- Revert `crates/sim/src/solid_rest.rs` to `upstream/main`: red (`thread major ride Z63..Z78: rest 0.8218 > gate 0.05625`); restore: green.\n- Revert `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/scan_turned.rs` and `scan_hidden.rs` to `upstream/main`: red (`thread major ride Z63..Z78: rest 2.3735 > gate 0.05625`); restore: green.\n\nAdditional mutation for the heavy-lane correction:\n- Restore `crates/sim/src/solid_rest.rs` from `upstream/main`: RED. The convex-cap pin finds two zero-width intervals at `(5, 5)` instead of one material interval.\n- Restore the PR file: GREEN. The corrected heavy pin and the true hidden-rest control both pass.\n\nGates on final head `d19a630355c0d30d1780a66c6283a3ced77f9c02`, base `upstream/main` at `58cb641caa0a4c0b6d514c3e874ccaee1b8a6e5b`:\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: GREEN. Motion and app lanes ran. All 220 steps passed in 29.7 minutes. Motion: 56 test passes. App: 42 test passes. The gate separately checked three known-fail tests for #1950. Each failed as expected. There were no unexpected failures.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN. All 7 steps passed. Sim lib: 195 passed. `hidden_rest_banded`: 5 passed, 1 ignored. `scan_arc`: 2 passed. `turned_hidden_rest`: 6 passed. `turning_hidden_floor`: 7 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: GREEN. No warnings.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full workspace batch and full release gates did not run. The reached motion and app heavy lanes ran and passed.\n- The GUI did not open a turning project.\n- The example catalog case `turning/cone-thread` (#2394 / PR #2883) is not on `main` yet and was not rebuilt here.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone.\n\nChangelog: Turning: Profile Finish and zero-leave Profile Rough no longer report false hidden rest on modelled thread valleys or on a neck step at the window boundary.\n\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #2880\n",
